<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450415" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 9 — Multiple consecutive tables with no paragraph between them</title>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d779e7">
         <p>Consider a section where two or more <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> elements appear one after another in the HTML source with no <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element between them.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Consecutive tables, no paragraph in between</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_jdc_twn_lkc">
&lt;h2 id="server-configuration">
  Server Configuration
&lt;/h2>
&lt;table>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;th>Parameter&lt;/th>
    &lt;th>Value&lt;/th>
  &lt;/tr>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>Port&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>8080&lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>Timeout&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>60&lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
&lt;/table>
&lt;table>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;th>Parameter&lt;/th>
    &lt;th>Value&lt;/th>
  &lt;/tr>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>Max connections&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>100&lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>Retry limit&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>3&lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
&lt;/table></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_rg4_ywn_lkc">
&lt;reference id="server_configuration">
  &lt;title>Server Configuration&lt;/title>
  &lt;refbody>
    &lt;simpletable>
      &lt;sthead>
        &lt;stentry>Parameter&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>Value&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/sthead>
      &lt;strow>
        &lt;stentry>Port&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>8080&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/strow>
      &lt;strow>
        &lt;stentry>Timeout&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>60&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/strow>
    &lt;/simpletable>
    &lt;simpletable>
      &lt;sthead>
        &lt;stentry>Parameter&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>Value&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/sthead>
      &lt;strow>
        &lt;stentry>Max connections&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>100&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/strow>
      &lt;strow>
        &lt;stentry>Retry limit&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;stentry>3&lt;/stentry>
      &lt;/strow>
    &lt;/simpletable>
  &lt;/refbody>
&lt;/reference></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b> Each HTML <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element is converted independently into a separate DITA <codeph>&lt;simpletable&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element. The converter does not automatically merge consecutive tables.</p>
         <note type="tip"> If the tables are logically related, add a short bridging <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element between them in the HTML source before conversion.</note>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
